     1	# Run statement — ATEN-only GEMM backend A/B (correctness above the int32 bound + component timing), single GPU, ≤ 45 min
     2	
     3	**Label: infrastructure diagnostic.** This run changes one Inductor setting, `torch._inductor.config.max_autotune_gemm_backends`, from torch 2.9.0's default `"ATEN,TRITON,CPP"` to `"ATEN"`. It changes no model, loss, reward or learning code. Adopting it would be an **infrastructure deviation from Isaiah's default backends**, not a learning change. The timing half is a **component measurement conditional on the A/B/C/D synthetic schedule** of `model-sps-ceiling.md`, not end-to-end SPS.
     4	
     5	- **Question (owner):** can v3 be made immune to the torch 2.9 compiled-GEMM int32 overflow (`cookbook/references/compiled-gemm-template-overflows-above-2-21-rows.md`; `results.md` "GEMM limits at our shapes")? **Hypothesis:** with `max_autotune_gemm_backends = "ATEN"`, every compiled mm/addmm lowers to extern cuBLAS (`extern_kernels.mm/addmm/bias_addmm`, 64-bit indexing), so the vulnerable Triton mm/addmm template class (and the persistent-TMA and decompose-K templates) is never generated, while the other Inductor fusions (pointwise, norms, reductions) stay Triton.
     6	- **Source reading supporting the hypothesis (installed pod torch 2.9.0+cu128, git `0fabc3ba…`, read over SSH before launch):** `_inductor/utils.py:1628–1631` `_use_autotune_backend` splits `config.max_autotune_gemm_backends`; `use_triton_template` (`utils.py:1640–1665`) requires `_use_autotune_backend("TRITON")`. In `kernel/mm.py` `tuned_mm` (760–783) and `tuned_addmm` (997–1029), the mm template, `persistent_tma_mm_template`, `decompose_k_subgraph_template` and the contiguous-subgraph templates are all added only inside `if is_nonzero and use_triton_template(...)`; ATEN choices come from `use_aten_gemm_kernels()` (`utils.py:2112–2115`). CUTLASS is not in the default list; CPP applies to CPU only. `tuned_bmm` (`kernel/bmm.py:200–211`) is gated the same way. Source reading is not a measurement; the run checks it.
     7	- **Expected discriminating observations:**
     8	  1. ATEN-only, guard bypassed: **every** listed case matches eager (below), where default backends previously corrupted or faulted. A single wrong element, non-finite value, crash or backend-record mismatch refutes "immune at these shapes" and stops the driver.
     9	  2. ATEN-only generated wrappers call only `extern_kernels.mm/addmm/bias_addmm` for GEMMs, contain **zero** `triton_tem_` kernel definitions or launches, and no decompose-K / persistent-TMA / contiguous-subgraph template text; the default-backend caches from the same run do contain `triton_tem_` launches (analyzer positive control).
